{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact Register 26 live record head e4f26d835a9a992273e1361b3a167dc62b0d86bc on planner/demo-r26-record-20261107, three paths, for request ba5e2a8d under promise 622a45c6 and review request e6bdc041. Every claim that I checked holds. The evidence units are not sealed, and one checksum file cannot pass its own check.\n\nRequired:\n\n1. Make the 56 evidence files read-only. The request calls the three units sealed, but every file in the manifest is writable: 39 files are 0644 and 17, including timeline.txt, are 0600. Run chmod a-w on each listed file. A mode change keeps every manifest size and digest, so this fix alone needs no new head.\n2. Fix 2026-11-07-demo-r26-room-reads/SHA256SUMS. It has 13 lines for 13 files, because it lists its own digest. `shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS` therefore reports \"./SHA256SUMS: FAILED\", and that line can never match. Remove the self-entry, then update that file's size and digest in the manifest. That fix needs a new head. The other two SHA256SUMS files list every file except themselves and pass.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main e50d9eeb is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds one commit and is pushed. The commit-message check passes for that commit. The commit changes only the record, its manifest and docs/deploy.md. No source, test, Wrangler file, dependency or seal changes.\n- Evidence. The manifest lists 56 files in three units, and each unit directory holds exactly its listed files. Every file matches its size and SHA-256. The credential scan finds no match. The paired probe passes the credential through GIT_CONFIG environment entries, never through arguments. It refuses to print a stderr line that contains the secret.\n- Settings. The private rendered files hash to 7c33b0cd… (install) and 14fb81a1… (offer), as the record states. Compared with apps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc at e50d9eeb, the offer file differs only in `main` and four variables: REGISTER_SCOPE, INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, ARTIFACTS_CONFIG and DEMO_START_CONFIG. The ARTIFACTS_CONFIG difference is only registerScope. The record's DEMO_START_CONFIG string equals the deployed value. The install file differs from the offer file only in DEMO_START_CONFIG.\n- The switch. timeline.txt records the plan at 00:05:28, the install deploy ending at 00:06:33, the install at 00:06:36 and the offer deploy ending at 00:08:20, all exit 0. 08-checks.txt shows three health answers from ab0f3784 with sessions ok, register ready and Artifacts wired. It also shows the offer on sc_zm56yco5… under platform:register@26 with host artifacts, namespace dap-demo and policy open, and POST /mcp 404. The dap-grow and dap-lending outputs show d10ef108 and 721cb866, written at 00:03 and 00:04.\n- Old rooms. The section matches acts 72e9b1f5, d9a635d2, ec5b86e0 and 0687e0f4, and it keeps the two deployments apart.\n- The scratch room. 10-create.stdout names the four scopes, their definitions and the Inbox. The Inbox genesis read at 13:15:14 UTC shows the open item and @failedclaimwitness as its owner party, and it names no definition. The record states the Inbox definition as an inference, not a read, and that is correct.\n- Token attempt 1. Act :8 is a read-token act at 13:15:34.549 UTC with fields {} and one grant, and its outcome :9 confirms it. 11-before.stderr shows the observer's host assertion failing inside archiveRun before any Git call. So the credential never reached Git.\n- Token attempt 2. Act :10 is at 13:16:35.566 UTC and its outcome :11 at 13:16:36.137 UTC. 12-before.json records the end time 14:16:36.137Z, the Artifacts remote, and the clone and journal fetch at exit 0. The clone holds only refs/heads/main at 1c94252. The replay refused with \"offline archive command could not complete within its bounds\". The diff of the observer copy changes only the two host assertions.\n- After the hour. The digest check passed. 15-after.json records Git exit 128 at 14:17:11.639Z, 35 seconds after the end time, and no new token.\n\nThe packet's condition. The packet requires retained provider refusal output for a nonzero after-phase exit. The after phase alone does not meet it, and the record says so. The paired probe meets it, for three reasons. It runs 58 seconds later with the same retained credential, whose digest passed. It targets the same remote. Its stderr carries the server's own line \"remote: Invalid or expired token\" with HTTP 403. The no-header control gets an authentication challenge instead, and the same Git client cloned with this credential an hour earlier. The probe uses ls-remote, not clone, so it shows the provider's answer to the expired credential, not the exact clone's answer. I accept that, because both commands send the same credential in the same request header.\n\ndocs/deploy.md. The example now names apps/room/wrangler.grow.jsonc and adds the dap-demo limit. The Commons line now says that existing dap-demo rooms stay on Register 17 and new rooms use Register 26. Both match the deployed configuration.\n\nArchitecture: no finding. The record changes no behavior. It keeps the two deployments, the two observers and every failed attempt apart, and it claims no parent acceptance.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The record and the evidence hold no credential. The probe keeps the credential out of arguments and output.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n\n1. The unit 2026-11-06-demo-register-cutover also holds the 7 November scene files, and timeline.txt gives times without dates, with the 09:17:12 qualification line after the 09:18:10 line. Give each 7 November line its date when you rewrite it, or put new scenes in a unit named for their day.\n2. The \"115 scopes, 13 rooms, one register\" line rests on 00-census.stdout, which shows only rows 115. The room and register counts come from 9f4eb5f1. Cite that act beside the census row.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d3b82d4961428ced24bb